; 11-prove-a-statement-by-induction.kurt
;
; Prove a statement by induction
;
; `natural.kurt` provides the induction principle. Supply the base case and induction step as one
; conjunction, because application of the induction rule is a single inference step.

load natural
bool P
arity P 1
const P

use P(0) and (forall $n in Nat (P($n) implies P($n + 1)))  "base-and-step"

forall $n in Nat P($n)
forall $n ($n in Nat implies P($n))
5 in Nat implies P(5)

; For a real proof, derive the base and step in a preceding proof block instead of introducing
; them with `use`. Keep the resulting conjunction available as one fact before invoking induction.
